# Shell scripts and the config files they source must keep LF endings whatever
# the platform they are checked out on. A CRLF checkout on Windows makes bash
# fail with "syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r'" the moment one of them
# is run through WSL or Git Bash — a failure that says nothing about the cause.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.env   text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf

# Test inputs are compared byte for byte or matched by FileCheck.
*.mlir  text eol=lf
*.dsl   text eol=lf
